 "gossip": {
  "text": "Darren, the bug has gone. Joe Burrow was a full participant at practice for the second straight day and says he expects to be at full strength for Monday night in Washington. Yesterday this column wondered whether his illness might turn into something. It turned into nothing, and that's bad news for Rob, who holds the Chiefs against Darren's Bengals at 38 percent. On the same day Kansas City ruled out Kenneth Walker III with his groin, along with guard Trey Smith (concussion) and tackle Jaylon Moore (ankle). Both teams are 7-2, but the bookies now have Cincinnati at 9.5-to-1 for the title, just shorter than the Chiefs at 9.7. My view is simple. A healthy quarterback with his blockers intact beats a team missing its running back and two linemen. Rob's 38 percent looks like the most he'll ever have. The Chiefs are still 16.5-point favourites over Arizona and the line hasn't moved. After yesterday, I'm not reading anything into that.\n\nSteve, those Chiefs injuries hit you too. Your coin flip with Andy now comes down to whose team falls apart more slowly.\n\nMeanwhile the Humphrey affair has gone celebrity. Carmelo Anthony has challenged him to do more than apologise for calling Baltimore \"best at making criminals.\" On the field, the Ravens go to Carolina without three defensive starters: Humphrey, Nnamdi Madubuike (hamstring) and Jaylinn Hawkins (knee). They're 250-to-1 for the title. Rob and Darren hold them in four bets between them, each at 8 or 10 percent. That isn't a position. It's a support group.",
